https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nSrEcPdA0hE     (Capo 2) (MC0)

TIP:  There are several versions of this old standard done by many different performers and each has their own take on the lyrics and the order of them.  The one presented here is by Boxcar Willie.  The starting note for singing is D (open 4th string) and remember the melody climbs to a peak on "ocean". 

TIP:  The intro begins with a three note walk-up picked quickly on the 5th string at the 2nd, 3rd, and 4th frets before the first (G).  (Notes may or may not transpose.)

TIP:  The opening line of each verse is a steady ascending march.  For example, in the first verse from "From ... to" and the second vers from "Our ... dandy".
       
 
